/* PH-80 E80-3 / D-013 §2 negative: `.ptr` is the raw implementation field.
 * Reading it would bypass the read-only `.data` view and `cstr()`, so it is a
 * hard error for every caller outside the built-in layer. */


int main(void)
{
    String s = "abc";
    printf("%s\n", s.ptr);
    return 0;
}
